---
/* Component — PageFooter
 * The page's footer bar. Each direct child of the slot becomes one column, laid
 * out in a row by the grid below; PageFooterColumn stacks its own contents.
 *
 * grid-auto-flow: column means columns are created as children arrive rather
 * than declared up front, so the footer takes however many PageFooterColumns it
 * is given without the component knowing the count — which it could not learn
 * anyway, since Astro slots are opaque.
 *
 * align-items: start keeps columns top-aligned rather than stretched, so a tall
 * column does not drag the others' content down with it.
 *
 * A full-width edge-to-edge band like PageHeader: as a direct child of Page
 * (outside PageBody's inline inset) it spans the whole window width on its own,
 * and the sunken fill bleeds edge to edge with it, while this rule's inline
 * padding insets the column content — without shrinking the element's own box
 * — so it caps at --bravoixr-page-max and lines up with the page column above.
 * Themes with the page via the semantic dark override. */
---

<footer>
  <slot />
</footer>

<style>
  footer {
    display: grid;
    grid-auto-flow: column;
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--bravoixr-spacing-10);
    padding-block: var(--bravoixr-spacing-5);
    padding-inline: max(var(--bravoixr-spacing-10), calc((100% - var(--bravoixr-page-max)) / 2));
    background: var(--bravoixr-color-surface-sunken);
  }
</style>
